  "helpTitle": "Help & how to use",
  "helpIntro": "Tap a topic to read how it works.",
  "helpStartTitle": "Getting started",
  "helpStart1": "On the home screen, tap Camera to take a photo or Gallery to pick one. Batch cuts out many photos at once.",
  "helpStart2": "Every photo opens in Crop & Rotate first, then in the editor. Your original photo is never changed.",
  "helpStart3": "When you are happy, tap Export in the editor. Recent Exports on the home screen lists everything you have exported.",
  "helpCropTitle": "Crop & Rotate",
  "helpCrop1": "Turn the photo left or right in 90° steps, and drag the frame to choose the part you want to keep.",
  "helpCrop2": "Free lets you shape the frame as you like. 1:1, 4:5 and 9:16 lock its shape. Tap Continue to open the editor.",
  "helpCutoutTitle": "Cut-out",
  "helpCutout1": "When the editor opens, PhotoSur finds the main subject and removes the background automatically, on your phone. No internet is needed.",
  "helpCutout2": "Edge Smoothness softens the edge of the cut-out, from 0 to 20 pixels.",
  "helpCutout3": "The eye button at the top shows your original photo so you can compare. Tap it again to go back. The brush is paused while the original is shown.",
  "helpCutout4": "For difficult subjects such as glass, shoes, bags and bottles, tap Get HD cut-out. The HD model downloads once, stays on your phone and then works offline. Once it is installed, every new cut-out uses it automatically. To redo the photo you have open, tap Redo cut-out in HD.",
  "helpBrushTitle": "Brush",
  "helpBrush1": "Erase removes parts of the subject. Restore brings back parts the cut-out removed.",
  "helpBrush2": "Drag one finger to paint. Use two fingers to zoom, up to 8 times, and to move the photo. The brush keeps its size on screen, so zooming in gives finer control.",
  "helpBrush3": "Brush Size goes from 1 to 50. Opacity sets how strongly each stroke applies.",
  "helpBrush4": "Undo and Redo step through your brush strokes. Reset clears all brush strokes and goes back to the automatic cut-out; it asks you to confirm first.",
  "helpBackgroundTitle": "Background",
  "helpBackground1": "Choose what goes behind your subject: transparent, white, black, a gradient, a colour, a blurred copy of your photo, or your own photo.",
  "helpBackground2": "Only one background is used at a time. Your latest choice replaces the earlier one.",
  "helpBackground3": "Add custom background lets you pick a photo from your gallery. Custom color opens a colour picker. The Blur slider goes from 0 to 25.",
  "helpBackground4": "Transparent shows a checkerboard while you edit. Export as PNG to keep it transparent.",
  "helpTemplatesTitle": "Templates",
  "helpTemplates1": "Templates are ready-made backgrounds in five groups: Studio, Color block, Textures, Light & shadow, and Gradients & patterns. Five scenes are shown in the panel; tap the Templates button to see them all.",
  "helpTemplates2": "Choosing a template works like choosing your own photo as the background: it replaces your earlier background choice.",
  "helpLayoutTitle": "Layout",
  "helpLayout1": "Drag the subject on the photo to move it. Pinch with two fingers to resize it.",
  "helpLayout2": "Choose Original, 1:1, 4:5 or 9:16 to set the shape of the final picture.",
  "helpLayout3": "Size sets how big the subject is, from 20% to 300%. Shadow sets how strong its shadow is. Auto-center puts the subject back in the middle. Reset undoes moving and resizing.",
  "helpLayout4": "This shape is used when the export size is Original. If you choose a size preset or a marketplace in the export sheet, that decides the final shape instead.",
  "helpExportTitle": "Export",
  "helpExport1": "Tap Export to open the export sheet. Nothing is applied until you tap Save to Gallery or Share, so you can change your choices as often as you like.",
  "helpExport2": "PNG keeps transparency. JPG makes smaller files but cannot be transparent, so a transparent background becomes white. WEBP is a small modern format; if your phone cannot make it, the file is saved as JPG. For JPG and WEBP, the Quality slider trades file size for detail.",
  "helpExport3": "Original keeps your photo’s size, with the shape chosen in Layout. 1:1 is 1080 × 1080, 4:5 is 1080 × 1350 and 9:16 is 1080 × 1920. Custom lets you type a width and height in pixels.",
  "helpExport4": "Marketplace presets set size, format and quality: Amazon 2000 × 2000 JPG, eBay 1600 × 1600 JPG, Etsy 2667 × 2000 JPG kept under 1 MB, and Shopify 2048 × 2048 PNG. Choosing one replaces your format and size choices, and choosing a format or size afterwards switches the marketplace off. Marketplace rules can change, so check your marketplace’s current requirements.",
  "helpExport5": "Amazon also uses a pure white background with no shadow and fits the subject to fill most of the frame. Your background choice in the editor is not changed. The other marketplaces keep your background.",
  "helpExport6": "Save to Gallery and Share both save the picture to your gallery and to Recent Exports. Share also opens your phone’s share menu. If saving to the gallery is not possible, the share menu opens instead. After exporting you return to the home screen.",
  "helpExport7": "Unless you have removed ads, an ad can appear after an export, at most once every two minutes.",
  "helpBatchTitle": "Batch",
  "helpBatch1": "Batch cuts out up to 30 photos in one go. Tap Batch on the home screen and pick your photos. The back button is turned off while a batch runs.",
  "helpBatch2": "All photos in a batch share one setup: one background and one marketplace. You cannot choose differently for each photo.",
  "helpBatch3": "Backgrounds work as in the editor: your own photo, a colour, a template, white, transparent, black, blur or a gradient. Only one applies, and your latest choice replaces the earlier one.",
  "helpBatch4": "The file format is chosen for you. With a marketplace, the photos follow that marketplace’s size and format. Without one, a transparent background gives PNG and any other background gives JPG, at the original size.",
  "helpBatch5": "Choosing Amazon switches the background to White; if you then choose another background, Amazon is switched off. eBay, Etsy and Shopify keep your background, but a JPG cannot be transparent, so it gets a white background.",
  "helpBatch6": "If the HD model is installed, every photo in the batch is cut out with it. The Get HD cut-out button next to Templates downloads it.",
  "helpBatch7": "Each photo is saved to your gallery and to Recent Exports as soon as it finishes. Stop ends the batch after the current photo, and photos already finished stay saved. If a photo fails, the batch carries on and tells you how many could not be processed. Done takes you back to the home screen; it does not save anything.",
  "helpLibraryTitle": "Your exports",
  "helpLibrary1": "Recent Exports on the home screen shows your latest exports. Tap See all for every export, grouped as Today, Yesterday, This week and Earlier.",
  "helpLibrary2": "Tap an export to open it full screen. Swipe to move between exports and pinch to zoom. The bar at the bottom has Share, Save to Gallery, Edit again and Delete.",
  "helpLibrary3": "The three-dot button on a tile opens the same actions. Edit again opens the exported picture as a new photo, so earlier brush strokes are not restored.",
  "helpLibrary4": "Select lets you choose several exports to share together or delete. Delete all exports removes every export from this phone.",
  "helpLibrary5": "Deleting removes exports from PhotoSur only. Pictures already saved to your gallery are not affected. The bottom of the See all screen shows how much space exports use on this phone.",
  "helpPrivacyTitle": "Privacy & ads",
  "helpPrivacy1": "Your photos are processed on your phone and are not uploaded. There is no account and no watermark.",
  "helpPrivacy2": "PhotoSur is free with every feature included, supported by ads. A banner appears at the bottom of some screens, and an ad can appear after an export.",
  "helpPrivacy3": "Go Ad-Free in Settings is a one-time purchase that removes the ads. It does not unlock anything else, because every feature is already free. Restore Purchases brings it back on a new phone.",
  "helpSettingsTitle": "Settings",
  "helpSettings1": "Theme can follow your phone, or be Light or Dark. Language changes the language of the app. Both are also in the home screen header.",
  "helpSettings2": "Edit reminders: if you leave the app with an unfinished edit, PhotoSur can remind you three hours later. Switch this off in Settings.",
  "helpSettings3": "HD cut-out model shows whether it is installed. Remove deletes it from your phone to free space; you can download it again at any time.",
  "helpSettings4": "Replay intro shows the welcome screens again. Support opens the support page. Animated home background turns the moving picture at the top of the home screen on or off.",
  "helpFixTitle": "If something goes wrong",
  "helpFix1": "If the automatic cut-out cannot run on a very old or low-memory phone, the brush still works, so you can finish the picture by hand.",
  "helpFix2": "If the HD download stops, check your connection and try again. It continues where it left off.",
  "helpFix3": "For anything else, open Support from Settings."
}
